{"ts": "2026-10-26T23:51:07.512440Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T2348Z-9953", "unit": "openspec:add-e2e-stack", "seq": 34, "type": "task.started", "task": "5.3", "title": "5.3 Write `test/support/e2e-stack/main.test.ts` first (spawn `process.execPath` on `test/support/e2e-stack/main.ts` with free `E2E_PORT` and `E2E_CONTROL_PORT`, temp `E2E_DATA_DIR` and `TMPDIR`: read the child's first stdout line and assert it equals `e2e stack ready on http://127.0.0.1:<E2E_PORT> control http://127.0.0.1:<E2E_CONTROL_PORT>`, failing at once on any other first line; then `/health` with `checks.db` `\"ok\"`, SIGTERM and exit code 0, the whole stdout being that line plus a newline, the empty data directory and no `postmaster.pid`; then a second child that gets SIGTERM as soon as a `ursitoare-e2e-*` directory appears in `E2E_DATA_DIR`, with exit code 0, empty stdout and an empty data directory; then `E2E_PORT=abc` and a busy port, both exit code 1 with the stderr text) and `e2e/test_e2e_stack.py` (every test marked `@pytest.mark.milestone(\"M0\")`, taking the `e2e_profile` fixture and calling `pytest.skip` when it is not `\"fake\"`, where unset means `fake`: `test_health_reports_database_ok`, `test_control_paths_are_not_on_the_engine_port` (stdlib `urllib.request.Request(url, method=...)` with no `data` and no `Content-Type` for `POST /reset`, `POST /faults` and `DELETE /faults` on `base_url`; the status is `err.code` of the caught `urllib.error.HTTPError` and the body must hold `NOT_FOUND`; a `URLError` such as a refused connection is not caught, so it fails the test), an `injected_fault` fixture (POST `{\"method\":\"GET\",\"url\":\"/health\",\"status\":503}` to `E2E_CONTROL_URL` or `DEFAULT_CONTROL_URL`, DELETE in teardown), `test_injected_fault_fails_the_route`, `test_fresh_state_clears_faults`, `test_fresh_state_is_a_noop_on_the_stack_profile` and `test_fresh_state_reports_an_unreachable_control_url`, the last two with `monkeypatch.setenv` and `request.getfixturevalue(\"fresh_state\")`), then replace `test/support/e2e-stack/main.ts` (the only task that changes it): first replace `process.stdout.write` with a forwarder to `process.stderr` and keep the original for the ready line (design.md decision 11), install the SIGTERM and SIGINT handlers, parse the variables, call `startE2eStack`, print the ready line, close on the first signal (when it came during the start: after the start settles, with no ready line) and `process.exit(0)` (`1` when close rejects), and print `e2e stack failed: <code> <message> <JSON of details>` to stderr with exit code 1 on any start error; and add `DEFAULT_CONTROL_URL` and the function-scoped `fresh_state` fixture to `e2e/conftest.py` (the only task that changes it; stdlib `urllib` with `ProxyHandler({})`, POST with no body and no `Content-Type`, 60 s timeout, `RuntimeError` naming the URL and carrying `error.code` and `error.details` of an envelope), leaving `e2e/test_health.py` unchanged, implementing requirements \"The stack process starts offline and stops on SIGTERM\", \"fresh_state resets the stack on the fake profile\" and \"The browser gate sees the database and not the control routes\""}
